      "side": 1,
      "message": "AIDL enums don\u0027t become Rust enums (they come out as `MyEnum(i32)` with associated constants for the variants), but AIDL unions seem worse -- they come out as enums where *each variant* has an associated value.\n\n```rust\npub enum Error {\n  OK(i32),\n  OPERATION_NOT_SUPPORTED(i32),\n  INVALID_SIGNATURE(i32),\n  INVALID_EC_KEY(i32),\n}\n```\n\nMore completely:\n- C++: https://paste.googleplex.com/4526116403412992\n- Rust: https://paste.googleplex.com/6550495886835712",
